  "body": "## Summary\n\nSeveral classes store `std::function` members, violating memory-rules §6 / GRAVE-05. None of these are hot paths — they are set once at boot or are stack-scoped with SBO-sized captures — so the practical fragmentation risk is low. Filing for consistency with the framework's own rules.\n\n| Site | Notes |\n|---|---|\n| `include/types/FetchContext.hpp:33` — `DeadlineToken::_timeProvider` | Flagged by the audit (misattributed to `FetchContext`). Token is stack-scoped per fetch; only capture is `[this]` (fits SBO). Test code in `test/test_unit/test_dataManager/test_main.cpp:1064+` uses it for time injection. |\n| `include/interfaces/IPreconditionRegistry.hpp:35,38` — `EvalFn` / `DescribeFn` | **Public API.** Stored for device lifetime; allocated once at registration. |\n| `modules/OTAUpdateManager/OTAUpdateManager.hpp:411` — `_preRebootHook` | Set once. |\n| `lib/DisplayServiceHelper/DisplayServiceHelper.h:38-39` — `_saveCallback`, `_isOtaActive` | Set once. |\n| `lib/DeepStackExecutor/DeepStackExecutor.h:106` — `_currentWork` | Copies the caller's `std::function` per `run()`; check whether this can hold a pointer/reference instead of a copy. |\n\n**Severity: Low.**\n\n## Suggested approach\n\n- Convert each to `fn(void* ctx)` + `void* ctx` per memory-rules §6.\n- `DeadlineToken`: `uint32_t (*timeFn)(void* ctx)` + `void* timeCtx`; update the two unit tests.\n- `IPreconditionRegistry`: public API change — may warrant `needs-approach-review` and a consumer migration note; could be split into its own issue at triage.\n- Tighten `check_std_function_member` in `release-audit-checks.sh` if it did not catch all of the above (it currently matches only `std::function<...> _name;` in `.hpp`, so it misses the `using` aliases in `IPreconditionRegistry`).\n\n## Context\n\nGroup 1 release-audit report item 1 (\"FetchContext GRAVE-05 Violation\") — rated 🔴 Blocking by the audit; re-assessed as Low. The one significant violation is tracked separately (DataManag