  "body": "## Summary\n\nSeven bare `new` allocations remain in framework code. C++ exceptions are disabled in every `sdkconfig.*` (`CONFIG_COMPILER_CXX_EXCEPTIONS` not set), so allocation failure calls `abort()` rather than returning `nullptr`.\n\n| Site | When | Notes |\n|---|---|---|\n| `modules/BLEManager/BLEStack.cpp:608` — `new ClientCallbacks(providerId)` | **Runtime**, on BLE central client creation | Most worthwhile to fix: should post `postCentralConnectFailure(...)` and return false on failure. |\n| `modules/DataManager/DataManager.cpp:181` — `new FrameworkSecureClient()` | Boot | Line 182 dereferences immediately — needs a null check, not just `nothrow`. |\n| `modules/DataManager/DataManager.cpp:183` — `new WiFiClient()` | Boot | |\n| `modules/BLEManager/BLEStack.cpp:365` — `new ChainingCharCallbacks(...)` | Once per characteristic at server start | |\n| `modules/ButtonModule/ButtonModule.cpp:163,219,272` — `new ShimContext{...}` | Boot (button registration) | Could be a fixed-size array given bounded button count. |\n\n**Severity: Low.** Boot-time abort → reboot is a tolerable failure mode; only the BLE client path runs at runtime.\n\n## Suggested approach\n\n- Convert all seven to `new (std::nothrow)` with null checks and graceful degradation (log + fail the operation / mark the subsystem unavailable).\n- Consider static allocation for `DataManager` clients and `ButtonModule` shim contexts.\n- Note: `nothrow` alone does not make these paths OOM-safe — `std::vector::push_back`, `String`, and `std::string` also `abort()` on failure. Don't overclaim in the PR.\n\n## Context\n\nGroup 1 release-audit report item 3 claimed **106 files**; actual count of real bare allocations in `modules/`, `lib/`, `include/`, `src/` is 7 sites in 3 files. Three of the six files the report named (`DeviceCrypto.cpp`, `OTADownloadEngine.cpp`, `WifiManager.cpp`) have no bare `new` — `DeviceCrypto` already uses `nothrow`. See the separate issue on the audit check's false positives.\n",
