  "body": "## Summary\n\n`check_missing_nothrow()` in `.agents/skills/framework-expert/scripts/release-audit-checks.sh` (~line 327) produces a heavily inflated result. The Group 1 release-audit report cited **106 files** as a 🔴 blocker; the real number in framework code is **7 allocation sites in 3 files**.\n\nCauses:\n\n1. **Search scope** — it greps all of `$ROOT_DIR` for `*.cpp`, including `test/` (mocks and fixtures legitimately use bare `new`) and `tmp/`. Other checks in the script exclude `stubs` / `portal_assets`; this one doesn't.\n2. **Log strings match** — the `new [A-Z]` regex matches string literals such as `ESP_LOGD(..., \"Generated and firmly committed new MAC-derived ...\")` in `lib/DeviceCrypto/DeviceCrypto.cpp:52`. Only `//` comment lines are stripped, not string literals or `/* */` / ` * ` doc-comment lines.\n3. **Severity** — every hit is reported as FAIL at the same level, with no distinction between boot-time and runtime allocations.\n\nResult: files such as `DeviceCrypto.cpp`, `OTADownloadEngine.cpp`, `WifiManager.cpp` were reported as offenders despite having no bare `new`, and the finding was escalated to \"release blocker\".\n\n**Severity: Low** (audit tooling / DX), but it caused a mis-triaged release blocker.\n\n## Suggested approach\n\n- Restrict the scan to framework source dirs (`modules/ lib/ include/ src/`) or explicitly exclude `test/` and `tmp/`.\n- Match allocation syntax more strictly (e.g. `\\bnew[[:space:]]+[A-Za-z_][A-Za-z0-9_:<>]*[[:space:]]*[({[]`) and drop lines where `new` appears inside a string literal or ` * ` doc comment.\n- Report the actual file:line list so the report author can verify, rather than just a file count.\n- Also review `check_std_function_member` (see the GRAVE-05 cleanup issue): it misses `using X = std::function<...>` aliases.\n- The same report also recommended routing the OTA client \"through `KeyManager`\" — worth checking whether audit guidance in `guides/release-audit.md` contains that remediation text and correcting it.\n\n## Context\n\nFollow-up from investigating the Group 1 release-audit blocker report.\n",
